 "rules": "Regular election for a full term (2027-2033). Plurality winner in the general election (runoffs apply only to primaries). Four candidates: Michael Whatley (R), Roy Cooper (D), Shannon Bray (Libertarian), Michael Dublin (Green). In-person early voting ran October 15-31, 2026 at about 370 sites; under current state law, mail ballots must be received by 7:30 p.m. on Election Day. Polls close at 7:30 p.m. Eastern; early and mail votes are usually reported first on election night; county canvasses follow about 10 days later. Sources: https://www.ncsbe.gov/news/press-releases/2026/10/09/10-things-person-early-voters-know-north-carolina ; https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_United_States_Senate_election_in_North_Carolina",
